<title>ESTONIA: NOON RADIO HEADLINES - APRIL 17.</title>
<headline>NOON RADIO HEADLINES - APRIL 17.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the main headlines reported by Kuku Radio on Wednesday at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and cannot vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- The Baltic countries and Denmark started political consultations in Vilnius.</p>
<p>- The health of Prime Minister Mart Siimann was said to be good after a medical examination.</p>
<p>- Tallinn city board will discuss the establishment of a sales tax in June.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
